<!--
    cfgspawnabletypes.xml — Realistic Vehicle Overhaul
    ====================================================
    Controls what parts vehicles spawn WITH (attachments) and what is
    found INSIDE them (cargo).

    INSTALL PATH: mpmissions/dayzOffline.chernarusplus/db/cfgspawnabletypes.xml
    If you already have a cfgspawnabletypes.xml, MERGE the <type> blocks below
    into your existing file. Do not duplicate existing entries.

    PART ATTACHMENT PHILOSOPHY:
    Each vehicle part has a LOW spawn chance to make working vehicles rare:
      CarWheel        0.25  — needing all 4 means ~0.4% chance of full set
      CarBattery      0.15  — rare, must be scavenged
      SparkPlug       0.12  — rarest mechanical part
      CarRadiator     0.20  — uncommon
      HeadlightH7Bulb 0.30  — slightly more common (cosmetic only)

    CARGO PHILOSOPHY:
    Every vehicle is a loot box surprise. Cargo pools are 20-30+ items wide.
    Rarity tiers:
      Common    (0.30-0.50): Rags, rotten food, junk, paper
      Uncommon  (0.10-0.25): Canned food, sodas, bandages, rope, clothing
      Rare      (0.03-0.09): Pistols, medical, vehicle parts as cargo
      Very Rare (0.01-0.03): Rifles, quality military/survival gear

    VEHICLE CARGO PROFILES:
      Civilian Sedan/Hatchback  — food, clothing, occasional pistol
      Police variants           — higher pistol/ammo chance, police gear
      Offroad/Farm Hatchback    — tools, outdoor gear, building supplies
      Truck                     — industrial tools, building materials, rifle

    NOTE: chance values on <cargo> and <attachments> parent elements are the
    probability that the SLOT is filled at all. Item chance values are relative
    weights among items competing for that slot.
-->
